WEBVTT

00:12.950 --> 00:15.070
Musik Activation Report

00:15.070 --> 00:17.660
Musik Activation Report

00:24.310 --> 00:26.960
You want work, don't you?

00:26.960 --> 00:28.040
Can't you take it more seriously?

00:28.040 --> 00:30.050
I <i>am</i> serious.

00:30.510 --> 00:32.910
I mean, "Franz Schubert"?

00:32.910 --> 00:34.890
Write your real name, would you?

00:34.890 --> 00:35.800
It <i>is</i> my real name!

00:36.090 --> 00:38.110
And your job history...

00:38.110 --> 00:39.540
You used to be a teacher?

00:39.540 --> 00:41.190
Do you even have a license?

00:41.190 --> 00:42.040
A license?

00:42.040 --> 00:44.560
You don't have a teaching license, do you?

00:44.820 --> 00:47.940
I just want work, damn it!

00:48.400 --> 00:50.730
That's what they all say.

00:50.730 --> 00:52.870
My landlady won't stop nagging me.

00:52.870 --> 00:54.650
"Pay your rent! Get a job..."

00:54.960 --> 00:57.450
That's what they all say.

00:57.840 --> 01:00.390
I want to be with my beloved great Senpai.

01:00.690 --> 01:02.870
I don't want to leave!

01:03.100 --> 01:05.620
That's what they all say.

01:05.620 --> 01:08.610
How is it that a deadbeat, nonchalant,

01:08.610 --> 01:10.620
freak like him can live it up

01:10.620 --> 01:12.920
while I have to struggle so much?

01:12.920 --> 01:14.970
He isn't working, either.

01:14.970 --> 01:17.380
That's what they all say.

01:18.180 --> 01:18.920
Ugh!

01:18.920 --> 01:20.510
Anyway, my landlady—

01:23.970 --> 01:25.980
Did I catch a cold?

02:56.900 --> 03:01.110
12: "J. S. Bach"

02:57.770 --> 03:00.950
Beg me all you want, but no means no.

02:59.030 --> 03:02.410
Arkhe Corporation Hosts
28th  New Artist Audition
Participant Green Room

03:00.950 --> 03:02.410
Oh, come on.

03:02.630 --> 03:06.460
We just need to do as Bach-sama says.

03:06.460 --> 03:07.660
But...

03:07.900 --> 03:10.150
You're worried, too, aren't
you, Tchaiko-chan?

03:10.150 --> 03:15.300
How could those losers, Beethoven
and Mozart, meet his—

03:20.470 --> 03:24.220
I'm so awesome, Arkhe Corp actually
invited me to an audition.

03:24.460 --> 03:27.920
Who knows how they chose us, though.

03:27.920 --> 03:31.130
Well, duh, the great producer, JSB,

03:31.130 --> 03:33.600
sees potential in us. That's why.

03:33.600 --> 03:35.390
Wh-What the...

03:35.390 --> 03:37.460
Why is <i>he</i> here?

03:37.460 --> 03:39.230
Audition...

03:40.770 --> 03:42.340
The one from earlier?

03:43.100 --> 03:47.080
But Bach-sama told us to
leave them be for now.

03:47.080 --> 03:48.120
I know.

03:48.410 --> 03:51.180
Maybe they figured out that
we're messing with them,

03:51.180 --> 03:52.980
and now they're here to get back at us.

03:53.610 --> 03:55.850
We need to report to Bach-sama.

03:57.920 --> 03:58.640
Here.

04:00.310 --> 04:02.140
Why are we here?

04:02.140 --> 04:03.730
I told you...

04:03.730 --> 04:06.390
We got a letter saying
your guitar performance

04:05.720 --> 04:09.100
Arkhe Corporation
28th New Artist Audition Application

04:06.390 --> 04:09.100
caught the eyes of some big shot, remember?

04:09.350 --> 04:11.040
Hey, hey, check this out.

04:11.040 --> 04:14.230
Doesn't this logo look familiar?

04:14.770 --> 04:18.190
I told you, it's the company that
hosted the competition.

04:18.830 --> 04:21.170
Why are you even with us?

04:21.170 --> 04:22.990
Because it seemed fun.

04:22.990 --> 04:26.110
Wait, wasn't it just
Lud-kun who got invited?

04:26.110 --> 04:27.910
Why are you here with him?

04:28.150 --> 04:30.410
Oh, well, y'know...

04:30.950 --> 04:33.430
I'm like, Beethes-san's buddy, I guess?

04:33.430 --> 04:34.960
His manager?

04:34.960 --> 04:38.490
B-Beethes-san just can't take
care of himself without me.

04:41.100 --> 04:45.010
Am I thinking of making my
pro debut with Beethes-san?

04:45.010 --> 04:47.300
Or that it would be amazing if I could
become friends with Claskey Klasky?

04:47.300 --> 04:48.390
No, I'm not.

04:50.390 --> 04:52.080
Anyway...

04:52.080 --> 04:54.810
If the boss takes care of you,
you'll be a professional musician!

04:55.040 --> 04:58.150
And then we can get a million
views on video sites!

04:58.150 --> 05:01.530
And we can make a killing selling
CDs with tickets to a handshake event.

04:58.730 --> 05:01.280
Handshake
Ticket

05:01.530 --> 05:04.780
And then we can get
filthy-rich on royalties.

05:05.030 --> 05:07.030
Kanae will love it, too.

05:07.850 --> 05:08.900
Money...

05:11.030 --> 05:13.770
They may call you a genius,

05:13.770 --> 05:15.870
but you're still in debt.

05:15.870 --> 05:17.000
Pathetic.

05:17.250 --> 05:21.250
I am your employer.
Just be quiet and do as I say.

05:24.010 --> 05:25.700
What was that?

05:31.460 --> 05:34.810
I think I bought too much
at the bargain sale.

05:40.060 --> 05:41.520
I'm sorry.

05:42.160 --> 05:43.120
Here you are.

05:43.630 --> 05:45.280
Thank you.

05:49.700 --> 05:52.160
What's going on? Next!

05:52.160 --> 05:53.420
Beethes-san!

05:53.420 --> 05:55.590
Get ready!
Come on, buck up.

05:55.890 --> 05:58.540
Sorry, we'll start right away.

05:58.540 --> 06:01.660
You wait over there, Wolfgang-kun.

06:02.190 --> 06:02.880
Me?

06:03.130 --> 06:06.300
What was his name... Ludwig-kun?

06:06.300 --> 06:08.340
We're going to evaluate you one at a time.

06:08.620 --> 06:10.320
Right this way.

06:10.930 --> 06:11.720
Hey!

06:12.120 --> 06:15.590
He doesn't have anything to
do with that competition!

06:14.820 --> 06:18.040
I don't see you on the audition list.

06:18.040 --> 06:21.140
No, well, I'm like his buddy...

06:21.140 --> 06:22.360
His attendant.

06:22.360 --> 06:24.620
Wait here, then, attendant.

06:24.620 --> 06:25.650
Got it?

06:28.960 --> 06:31.450
Were you the one that invited them?

06:31.730 --> 06:32.450
Yes.

06:32.750 --> 06:34.250
What do you think you're doing?

06:34.250 --> 06:36.900
Are you going to defy the man's orders?

06:36.900 --> 06:38.370
Of course not.

06:38.600 --> 06:39.250
Then—

06:39.250 --> 06:42.460
"Bring all ClassicaLoids
to a complete state."

06:43.060 --> 06:45.450
Isn't that Bach-sama's goal?

06:45.450 --> 06:46.510
Well...

06:46.810 --> 06:48.590
I called those two in order

06:48.590 --> 06:51.430
to come closer to that goal.

06:52.030 --> 06:54.230
Well, just watch me.

06:59.040 --> 07:00.270
A guest?

07:03.710 --> 07:04.760
Why...

07:06.460 --> 07:09.380
Oh, really? My father?

07:09.820 --> 07:10.540
Yes.

07:10.990 --> 07:13.920
I'm greatly indebted to your father.

07:14.570 --> 07:17.520
I'm sorry you came all the way out here

07:17.520 --> 07:19.330
when my father isn't home.

07:19.620 --> 07:20.950
Not to worry.

07:20.950 --> 07:23.490
I'm sorry for coming unannounced.

07:23.490 --> 07:26.270
Oh, no. That's not a problem.

07:29.470 --> 07:31.430
This is quite unusual.

07:32.490 --> 07:34.630
That belonged to my grandmother.

07:35.090 --> 07:36.050
I see.

07:40.380 --> 07:42.800
Seeing this brings back memories

07:43.150 --> 07:46.070
of the instrument I used to play.

07:47.320 --> 07:49.800
Are you in the music business?

07:49.800 --> 07:50.660
Yes.

07:50.990 --> 07:52.970
Although I'm only a casual.

07:53.270 --> 07:54.450
A casual?

07:55.650 --> 07:58.090
I have yet to

07:58.610 --> 08:01.280
create real music.

08:01.890 --> 08:05.450
I hope to do so one day.

08:17.720 --> 08:19.620
Come on, Beethes-san.

08:19.620 --> 08:21.090
You got this.

08:21.090 --> 08:22.810
We need to earn those royalties.

08:23.950 --> 08:25.690
Who's texting me at a time like this?

08:25.690 --> 08:28.270
From: Chopin-san
To: CryingDarkAngel

08:26.790 --> 08:27.950
Chopin-san?

08:28.270 --> 08:30.460
Later!

08:31.410 --> 08:34.030
Are you interested in becoming an idol?

08:34.300 --> 08:35.200
An idol?

08:35.500 --> 08:36.280
Yeah.

08:36.280 --> 08:40.180
You look decent, and you're endearing.

08:40.180 --> 08:42.960
You could do pretty well, with our help.

08:44.290 --> 08:45.870
The girls will be all over you.

08:45.870 --> 08:46.710
All over me?

08:46.980 --> 08:47.770
Yup.

08:47.770 --> 08:51.390
Thousands, tens of thousands,
of girls will be obsessed with you.

08:51.390 --> 08:54.790
They'll spend all of their
allowance on you and

08:54.790 --> 08:57.820
go wild with every breath you
take, every move you make.

09:02.830 --> 09:05.830
Are you all getting your bl**p bl**ps on?

09:06.680 --> 09:08.210
Ble** ble**!

09:08.750 --> 09:09.930
Bl**p bl**p.

09:10.770 --> 09:12.140
Bl**p bl**p!

09:12.140 --> 09:14.780
All together now...

09:15.300 --> 09:16.790
Ble** ble**!

09:16.790 --> 09:18.410
Ble** ble**!

09:18.410 --> 09:20.580
Ble*p ble*p!

09:20.580 --> 09:21.320
Hm?

09:21.320 --> 09:24.320
I'll do it! I'll do it! I'm an idol!

09:26.150 --> 09:27.920
Music is a manifestation

09:28.490 --> 09:31.660
of the passions deep in the heart.

09:32.020 --> 09:35.090
In fact, you could say
it is the soul itself.

09:41.630 --> 09:43.240
H-How...

09:43.660 --> 09:46.850
Music is without shackles.

09:47.460 --> 09:50.630
It ought to be made freely,

09:50.930 --> 09:52.730
and it ought to be free.

09:53.540 --> 09:56.900
But in reality, it doesn't work that way.

09:57.320 --> 09:58.910
Is that so?

09:59.380 --> 10:00.090
Yes.

10:00.890 --> 10:03.580
One has to do what they want to do

10:03.580 --> 10:06.190
within the many rules and
constraints that exist.

10:06.750 --> 10:08.290
You can't just play anything

10:09.020 --> 10:12.050
you want to express.

10:13.580 --> 10:15.130
It's without purpose unless

10:15.430 --> 10:18.180
you make something that attracts an
audience—that creates demand.

10:18.990 --> 10:22.370
Even if that isn't what
you really want to do.

10:23.360 --> 10:26.060
It's far-removed from real freedom.

10:28.280 --> 10:31.770
Thus freedom is the opposite of nihilism.

10:32.490 --> 10:33.940
Ours is but a frail existence,

10:34.450 --> 10:36.440
meandering between absolute freedom

10:37.140 --> 10:39.450
and arbitrary restrictions.

10:43.050 --> 10:44.410
I'm sorry.

10:44.740 --> 10:47.660
That was a very dull thing
to hear for the uninterested.

10:47.970 --> 10:51.710
No, I'm sorry, I didn't really get it.

10:52.610 --> 10:54.540
I can tell

10:54.540 --> 10:58.340
you're in agony, though.

11:03.150 --> 11:04.350
I suppose.

11:05.040 --> 11:07.560
It may be that I've always been in agony.

11:17.820 --> 11:19.820
From Cho-chan

11:18.190 --> 11:19.820
Oh, Cho-chan.

11:20.440 --> 11:22.250
You can be so lonesome.

11:24.480 --> 11:26.450
Okay, stop there.

11:26.920 --> 11:29.140
Beethoven, was it?

11:30.170 --> 11:31.400
That's hilarious.

11:31.400 --> 11:33.670
You call yourself by the
same name as that genius?

11:33.670 --> 11:37.550
Your paperwork says you got a lot
of attention by being unusual.

11:38.220 --> 11:42.050
I've seen people like you, acting
like half-assed artists.

11:42.350 --> 11:45.580
Yet it's all trite imitations.

11:45.580 --> 11:46.810
Are you like that, too?

11:47.210 --> 11:49.480
Don't get the wrong idea.

11:50.210 --> 11:53.030
We invited you to this audition because,

11:53.030 --> 11:55.010
based on the records from the competition,

11:55.010 --> 11:57.570
you created a certain amount of buzz.

11:57.870 --> 12:00.650
If you want to make your
debut, if you want to sell,

12:00.650 --> 12:03.850
you'll have to follow our policies.

12:05.720 --> 12:07.160
I'm done.

12:07.160 --> 12:09.160
You're way too selfish.

12:09.420 --> 12:10.650
Selfish?

12:10.650 --> 12:12.530
Idols nowadays have to be able to

12:12.530 --> 12:14.830
dance some, or you'll never make it.

12:14.830 --> 12:16.790
I'm not interested in this dance.

12:17.080 --> 12:20.690
Also, you're not allowed to
talk negative like that.

12:20.690 --> 12:23.550
Blurt out the wrong thing,
and you'll cause a shit storm.

12:23.780 --> 12:24.810
Fine, fine.

12:24.810 --> 12:28.520
Also, you're a potty mouth.
No obscenities whatsoever.

12:28.520 --> 12:29.310
Potty?

12:29.560 --> 12:32.200
Like <i>#$*(@</i> or <i>$@&^</i> or <i>%$^&</i>.

12:32.200 --> 12:34.510
You'll make trouble on air.
No obscenities!

12:34.510 --> 12:35.400
Got it?

12:35.400 --> 12:36.700
No way.

12:36.700 --> 12:37.560
No obscenities!

12:37.560 --> 12:40.300
I'm quitting idol work, then.

12:39.580 --> 12:41.070
What?!

12:41.930 --> 12:43.490
U-Um...

12:44.620 --> 12:48.380
I don't really understand everything,

12:49.010 --> 12:52.750
but I think you can enjoy
music a little more.

12:53.740 --> 12:55.130
I'm sorry.

12:55.430 --> 12:57.690
I shouldn't speak when I don't know much.

12:58.140 --> 13:00.130
No, continue.

13:00.900 --> 13:03.220
I want to hear what you have to say.

13:03.630 --> 13:06.450
I don't really have much to say.

13:07.140 --> 13:09.470
It's just that we have several people

13:09.470 --> 13:11.650
here who play music or something.

13:11.990 --> 13:14.450
I was reminded of them.

13:15.380 --> 13:18.270
They're always doing whatever
the heck they want,

13:18.900 --> 13:21.530
but they always seem to be having fun.

13:25.220 --> 13:26.730
I'm sorry.

13:26.730 --> 13:28.020
Damn it, those guys...

13:28.020 --> 13:30.410
They make such a mess.

13:31.120 --> 13:34.430
You take care of them, do you?

13:34.430 --> 13:37.720
They're absolutely terrible when it
comes to anything other than music.

13:37.720 --> 13:41.670
I'm trying to get them to follow the
basic rules of living with other people.

13:42.800 --> 13:45.040
Moderate constraints, offering stimulation

13:45.340 --> 13:48.340
without corrupting freedom, huh?

13:50.370 --> 13:51.360
I see.

13:52.380 --> 13:55.520
This may indeed be a
comfortable place to be.

13:58.460 --> 14:00.970
I get that you're passionate,

14:00.970 --> 14:03.150
but that's getting old.

14:03.700 --> 14:05.980
Let's see, I think what you need is...

14:05.980 --> 14:06.970
That's enough.

14:06.970 --> 14:07.870
Shut up.

14:08.170 --> 14:08.910
What?

14:09.210 --> 14:12.960
It's clear that you lot
don't understand anything.

14:13.580 --> 14:15.600
You're so arrogant.

14:15.900 --> 14:17.510
Do you not want to make your debut?

14:17.510 --> 14:20.130
The first thing you need in
order to make your debut...

14:20.130 --> 14:22.430
Allow me to teach you

14:23.130 --> 14:27.130
what music truly is.

14:29.840 --> 14:32.270
Come on, let me go! I'm going home!

14:32.270 --> 14:33.200
You will not.

14:33.200 --> 14:36.190
We paid for your stylist and dance lessons.

14:36.190 --> 14:37.940
None of that comes for free.

14:37.940 --> 14:39.510
So what?

14:39.510 --> 14:42.740
If you're quitting, I'll make you
pay for everything you cost me.

14:42.740 --> 14:44.210
You aren't making any sense.

14:44.210 --> 14:45.820
Just listen to us.

14:46.060 --> 14:49.960
Just shut up and do as we say!

14:50.860 --> 14:53.470
They may call you a genius,

14:53.470 --> 14:55.550
but you're still in debt.

14:55.850 --> 14:57.080
Pathetic.

14:57.720 --> 14:59.860
Go back to Salzburg.

14:59.860 --> 15:01.260
But sir...

15:01.260 --> 15:03.210
You will not talk back to me.

15:03.690 --> 15:05.890
I am your employer.

15:05.890 --> 15:09.900
Just be quiet and do as I say.

15:10.430 --> 15:12.300
Just shut up and do as we say.

15:12.890 --> 15:14.300
For me.

15:14.550 --> 15:16.350
As we say.

15:17.640 --> 15:18.720
No more.

15:19.140 --> 15:21.260
No more!

15:21.260 --> 15:22.020
Stop!

15:22.390 --> 15:24.140
Don't you want to be an idol?

15:24.140 --> 15:28.240
I don't care anymore!

15:29.100 --> 15:30.450
I can't control my body!

15:30.990 --> 15:32.360
Stop me!

15:32.870 --> 15:34.130
More!

15:42.290 --> 15:45.290
Sorry you came all the
way out here for nothing.

15:45.860 --> 15:46.780
It's fine.

15:47.080 --> 15:50.970
Feel free to contact me if
there's anything you need.

15:51.620 --> 15:53.150
Thank you.

15:56.340 --> 15:57.470
My ride.

15:57.760 --> 15:59.640
It seems there's been an emergency.

16:04.390 --> 16:07.960
Perhaps they're best left
in that environment.

16:09.780 --> 16:13.770
I don't understand him,
but he was a good person.

16:15.120 --> 16:16.910
My little kitten!

16:17.190 --> 16:18.930
A-Are you okay?

16:29.520 --> 16:33.300
This <i>has</i> to be Beethes-san and Motes-san.

16:33.600 --> 16:35.350
How did this happen?

16:36.210 --> 16:38.350
I need to find them.

16:42.280 --> 16:44.100
Who are you?
Watch where you're going!

16:45.270 --> 16:46.350
Tchaiko-chan!

16:46.350 --> 16:47.270
Bąda-kyun?!

16:47.740 --> 16:49.890
Oh, err...

16:50.350 --> 16:51.680
Tool-san?

16:51.680 --> 16:53.740
That's not really my name.

16:53.980 --> 16:55.350
But sure.

16:55.350 --> 16:57.780
Anyway, uh...

16:58.180 --> 17:00.100
I know this isn't a good time, but...

17:00.500 --> 17:02.290
Can we

17:03.180 --> 17:04.750
exchange email addresses?

17:05.760 --> 17:06.990
S-Sure.

17:06.990 --> 17:07.700
Really?!

17:07.700 --> 17:08.840
Do it later!

17:08.840 --> 17:10.540
Doofus! Dumb-dumb!

17:23.630 --> 17:25.090
Tchaiko-chan...

17:26.330 --> 17:29.500
There're too many.
My Musik would be no match.

17:29.860 --> 17:31.520
Oh, no!

17:31.820 --> 17:33.990
This situation...

17:33.990 --> 17:35.860
I think I'm in luck!

17:51.520 --> 17:56.600
Fuege Dich zusammen meine Melodie!

18:26.920 --> 18:27.670
Huh?

18:28.020 --> 18:30.420
All right, here we go.

18:34.180 --> 18:35.780
It's them!

18:35.780 --> 18:37.460
They started this mess!

18:37.460 --> 18:39.890
Come on, you're the one that started it.

18:40.210 --> 18:44.160
Are you the leader of these fools?

18:49.850 --> 18:50.740
What?

18:50.740 --> 18:52.940
Are you a ClassicaLoid, too?

18:53.560 --> 18:56.580
Is this the music you make?

18:57.150 --> 19:00.030
You're an insult to true musicians.

19:00.700 --> 19:02.630
H-He just spoke normally!

19:02.630 --> 19:04.120
I've never heard him talk before!

19:04.480 --> 19:06.560
You make a mockery of music.

19:06.860 --> 19:10.120
You shackle us and attempt to extinguish
the flames of our passions.

19:10.420 --> 19:11.670
Fool!

19:11.670 --> 19:14.040
Music isn't any fun unless it's free.

19:15.700 --> 19:19.280
True music—true expression of the soul—Musik

19:19.730 --> 19:22.850
made from the whole of who I am.

19:23.140 --> 19:26.900
See how powerful it is!

19:27.930 --> 19:30.190
See mine, too.

19:36.750 --> 19:37.860
Passion?

19:38.090 --> 19:38.960
Freedom?

19:39.280 --> 19:40.280
Laughable!

19:41.030 --> 19:43.880
Passion and simple appetite
are two different things.

19:43.880 --> 19:46.730
So, too, do freedom and irresponsible
selfishness differ.

19:47.030 --> 19:49.040
You don't deserve to create music

19:49.310 --> 19:51.770
if you can't make that distinction!

19:52.740 --> 19:54.960
Bach-sama is great!

19:54.960 --> 19:55.990
Bach-sama!

19:55.990 --> 19:58.710
Wait, so that dude's <i>the</i> Bach?

19:59.060 --> 20:01.470
Bach? Him?

20:01.800 --> 20:03.630
A desire for freedom,

20:03.930 --> 20:06.940
a passion for music rising
from deep within...

20:07.230 --> 20:09.360
Those, in and of themselves, are true.

20:09.990 --> 20:13.850
But to run about wild makes you

20:14.190 --> 20:15.730
no different from animals.

20:16.130 --> 20:20.210
Music is like an arrow, shot with

20:20.510 --> 20:23.820
clear intent at a single target!

20:30.990 --> 20:33.030
To launch that arrow,

20:33.330 --> 20:37.250
we musicians must confront
pain and endure anxiety

20:37.250 --> 20:40.670
as we conjure the best music possible.

20:40.940 --> 20:42.800
What the hell are you talking about?

20:43.360 --> 20:46.790
You are not yet messengers of music.

20:47.440 --> 20:50.180
To create the Eight Sounds I seek...

20:51.260 --> 20:52.240
Eight Sounds?

20:52.810 --> 20:54.810
You need not know yet.

20:54.810 --> 20:57.990
For now, know that you are not ready.

21:06.930 --> 21:08.280
Wait, please.

21:08.540 --> 21:10.660
Why are we getting in trouble?

21:10.660 --> 21:12.910
Tch-Tchaiko-chan's right.

21:13.150 --> 21:14.720
We weren't the ones who called them.

21:14.720 --> 21:16.470
Man, I messed up.

21:16.470 --> 21:17.900
Sorry 'bout that.

21:18.460 --> 21:23.020
However, I think it's good that you got to see

21:23.020 --> 21:26.650
their progress first-hand, Bach-sama.

21:30.250 --> 21:33.480
I wonder why Bach let you come home.

21:33.480 --> 21:35.580
How should I know?

21:35.580 --> 21:37.330
He's being moody.

21:37.330 --> 21:40.480
Oh dear, are you <i>that</i> upset that you lost?

21:40.730 --> 21:41.940
Not really.

21:41.940 --> 21:43.710
Besides, we never lost.

21:43.710 --> 21:44.490
Right?

21:44.750 --> 21:47.690
No, that was utter defeat.

21:48.100 --> 21:51.910
We ought to admit our shortcomings
and strive to improve.

21:52.160 --> 21:53.710
That's my Senpai!

21:53.710 --> 21:56.740
Accepting reality and aiming higher.

21:56.740 --> 21:58.210
Unlike someone else I know.

22:04.680 --> 22:06.940
So you <i>don't</i> accept it.

22:06.940 --> 22:09.570
Hurry up and feed me!

22:09.570 --> 22:12.000
Fine, fine. It's ready.

22:12.000 --> 22:13.900
But only for Liszt-san and Chopin-san.

22:13.900 --> 22:14.770
Why?!

22:15.010 --> 22:17.730
You'll eat when you pay your rent.

22:17.730 --> 22:21.970
But Landlady, I intend
to both work and to pay rent!

22:21.970 --> 22:24.150
But the employers simply won't listen to me.

22:24.150 --> 22:25.940
Bąda-kyun

22:24.470 --> 22:25.940
"That's what they all say."

22:27.770 --> 22:28.950
"That's what they all—

22:32.840 --> 22:35.630
So <i>that</i> was Kyougo's daughter.

22:40.540 --> 22:42.650
I guess I might have a cold after all.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:25.730
13: "Die Forelle"

24:16.930 --> 24:20.920
Sinking into a bathtub, one
early, pleasant afternoon...

24:20.920 --> 24:24.010
It's heaven indeed.
Who could blame me for humming?

24:24.010 --> 24:25.730
But it was a huge mistake.

24:25.730 --> 24:28.610
Suddenly, my body is covered in scales,
and I'm taken away by a stream.
